+# YouTube Hunter Experimental v0.1
+
+This branch adds an experimental Morphe patch named **YouTube Hunter (Experimental)**.
+
+## Scope
+
+The first build is deliberately diagnostic-first and only acts on YouTube search-result cards.
+
+Settings added under Morphe > General > YouTube Hunter (Experimental):
+
+- Enable YouTube Hunter
+- Hunter diagnostic logs
+- Minimum duration (minutes)
+- Hide Shorts in search
+- Require auto-dub marker
+
+## Safety defaults
+
+All destructive filters default to OFF. Hunter itself also defaults to OFF. Unknown duration is fail-open in v0.1 so an unrecognized card is not accidentally hidden.
+
+## Runtime signals
+
+The filter inspects Litho search-card protobuf/ASCII content and logs:
+
+- video ID from thumbnail URL
+- duration-like tokens
+- known Shorts markers
+- Morphe auto-dub radar markers
+- component path and truncated accessibility/ASCII context
+
+## Goal of v0.1
+
+Install this build, enable Hunter + diagnostic logs, run a few YouTube searches, and use the logs to confirm the exact duration and audio metadata exposed by YouTube 21.37.42 before enabling stricter filtering.
+
+## Build note
+
+The source package is ready, but the current build environment could not download Gradle from services.gradle.org due blocked outbound DNS/network access. Build the `.mpp` in a network-enabled environment or GitHub Actions.
